      "source": "synthetic",
      "_note": "Synthetic in-bounds ELSYS TLV frame exercising every paired external bank on BOTH ports with distinct values. Raw decode confirmed via the ORACLE method against reference/upstream-codec.js: {temperature:21.5, humidity:55, co2:500, vdd:3600, analog1:1500, pulse1:7, pulseAbs:123456, externalTemperature:12.5, digital:1, pulse2:9, pulseAbs2:654321, analog2:3300, externalTemperature2:-1.5, digital2:0}. expected.data is the authored normalization: onboard temperature/humidity/CO2 -> air.* and VDD mV -> battery volts stay top-level (whole-device), while each port's bank readings are scoped into its own channels entry (port0 = Elsys port 1, port1 = Elsys port 2) under port-index-free key names. Upstream's unnumbered `pulseAbs`, `externalTemperature` and `digital` are port-1 aliases, hence their placement in port0."
